title: "KazistovVv: industrial robot control platform in Unity"
abstract: >-
  KazistovVv is an engineering environment for industrial manipulators built as a Unity
  application. It covers the full operator loop — aim, plan, preview, validate and execute —
  with a safety gate in front of every motion. The platform implements RRT / bidirectional
  RRT motion planning, time-optimal reparameterisation, forward and inverse kinematics,
  capsule-chain collision checking, joint limit and singularity validation, motion
  execution on the desktop, in VR, MR and AR, export to KRL / KAREL / RAPID and import
  from URDF / STEP. Two robot models are supported per scene: a six-axis arm and a SCARA.
  No AI model participates in motion: the pipeline is deterministic and reproducible from
  the action log. The software is proprietary; the source is published for reading and
  evaluation only.
